WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.310
From the origins of Optimus Primal and the
threat of Scourge, to the influence of the

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:08.360
'90s TV series "Beast Wars," here is all you
need to know before seeing "Transformers:

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.360
Rise of the Beasts."

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.053
"Transformers: Rise of the Beasts" hits theaters
in 2023.

00:00:13.053 --> 00:00:17.740
It was originally set to premiere on June
24, 2022, however, the seventh installment

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.670
of the robot franchise was bumped back by
almost a full year.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:25.130
Now, the film is set to be released on June
9, 2023, in the United States, Canada, and

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:26.130
the U.K.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.730
It will arrive in some European countries,
including Italy, France, and Iceland, a little

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.850
earlier, premiering on June 7.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:35.000
Other countries such as Australia and New
Zealand will have to wait a little longer,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.100
until June 22, to see the film.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.230
June 2023 will be a pretty crowded month for
blockbusters and tentpole movies.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:45.469
"Rise of the Beasts" will find itself competing
against some pretty awesome 2023 releases

00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:48.910
such as "Elemental," "Spider-Man: Across the
Spider-Verse," and "The Flash."

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:53.750
"Rise of the Beasts" has a comparable budget
to "The Flash," coming in at $200 million.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.400
But with the controversy surrounding the film's
lead, Ezra Miller, it's unclear how the highly

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.501
anticipated movie will fare.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:02.700
So, we'll be fascinated to see if "Rise of
the Beasts" can defeat its theatrical foes

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.000
and claim the title of the summer movie champion.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:09.220
"Rise of the Beasts" sees the Autobots and
Decepticons duking it out again, while also

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:13.120
ushering in new characters and a different
story to breathe life into the franchise.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:17.510
The seventh "Transformers" installment, which
is set in 1994, will follow a veteran named

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:21.619
Noah, a man who loves his family and is looking
for redemption for past mistakes.

00:01:21.619 --> 00:01:25.630
The female co-lead is named Elena, a museum
researcher whose knowledge of artifacts will

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.900
no doubt factor heavily into the plot.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.630
It's possible that through her work, she,
Noah, and the Autobots discover the existence

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:36.110
of three new tribes of Cybertronians: the
reptilian Predacons, the villainous Terrorcons,

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:39.610
and the heroic Maximals, who all make their
debut in this film.

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:43.630
While Optimus Prime and Bumblebee have often
been the most notable Autobots, taking the

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:47.600
lead in the original trilogy and the 2018
prequel respectively, it's Mirage who forms

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.540
the closest bond with the humans in this film.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.530
He'll likely be Noah and Elena's introduction
to the Autobots, the same way that Bumblebee

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:54.530
was for Sam Witwicky.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:58.830
The movie's official synopsis doesn't reveal
a lot, but it does confirm that the Maximals

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:03.490
will ally themselves with the Autobots in
a battle against the Terrorcons, Predacons,

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.490
and Decepticons.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:07.890
Since this is a prequel, we know that the
heroes don't succeed in wiping out the Decepticons,

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:11.530
but fan-favorite characters like Optimus Prime
and Bumblebee will live to fight another day.

00:02:12.118 --> 00:02:17.400
For the most part, the "Transformers" franchise
is Michael Bay's gigantic, explosive, musclebound baby.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.150
The blockbuster auteur helmed the first five
films of the franchise to huge box office

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.319
earnings and mixed critical acclaim.

00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:27.630
For the 2018 prequel, "Bumblebee," directing
duties were given to Travis Knight, who also

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:30.140
directed the animated film "Kubo and the Two
Strings."

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:34.690
Now, a third filmmaker will enter the franchise,
as Steven Caple Jr. is directing "Transformers:

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:35.830
Rise of the Beasts."

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:39.940
Caple made his feature-length directorial
debut with 2016's "The Land," a tale of four

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:44.142
teenage skateboarders earning the wrath of
a crime boss after stealing a car full of drugs.

00:02:44.142 --> 00:02:48.230
He followed that up with "Creed II," which
saw Michael B. Jordan's titular boxer grappling

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:50.870
with his past and battling a Russian bruiser.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.820
He's also worked on the TV shows "Rapture"
and "Grown-ish."

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.720
Speaking with Trey Mangum of "Shadow and Act,"
Caple explained what he's going for with "Rise

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.790
of the Beasts," saying,

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:00.970
"There's a lot of heart and emotion that I
draw from.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:05.170
If you've seen any of my work, I love to stay
grounded, even though the scope could be here

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:06.170
and we're blowing up stuff."

00:03:06.575 --> 00:03:11.220
At their core, "Transformers" stories are
about good versus evil, truth, freedom, the

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:14.849
importance of humanity, and doing the right
thing even when it's hard.

00:03:14.849 --> 00:03:18.220
These themes are showcased through unlikely
heroes like Sam, Cade, and Charlie.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:22.590
This will be the case again in "Rise of the
Beasts," and director Steven Caple Jr. has

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:26.250
made it clear he wants the movie to show that
heroes come in all different shapes and sizes.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:30.459
The entire creative team is in support of
this messaging and is keen to make sure audiences

00:03:30.459 --> 00:03:34.000
meet new heroes and aren't just getting another
version of the same old battle between the

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.340
Autobots and the Decepticons.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:39.590
Producer Lorenzo di Bonaventura teased during
an interview with "Collider,"

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:43.160
"I wanna start by saying that what we're trying
to do with this movie is to give the audience

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.280
a lot of new.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.090
If you've seen and been a fan of the other
movies, you're gonna see villains you've never

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:50.409
seen before, you're gonna see Autobots you've
never seen before, and you're gonna see a

00:03:50.409 --> 00:03:52.229
lot of elements that we've never done before."

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.020
"Rise of the Beasts" brings a lot of new elements
to the big screen franchise, but one constant

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:02.129
that viewers can count on is Peter Cullen
who is back voicing the Autobot Optimus Prime.

00:04:02.129 --> 00:04:05.629
As the strong and steady leader of the Autobots,
Optimus is the common thread throughout the

00:04:05.629 --> 00:04:06.819
"Transformers" franchise.

00:04:06.819 --> 00:04:10.709
But, leaning into that theme of new, viewers
are going to see a different side to him this

00:04:10.709 --> 00:04:11.709
time around.

00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:15.600
As a prequel, there's an opportunity for fans
to see Optimus grow as a character, since

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.978
at this stage, he's still figuring out his
place on Earth.

00:04:17.978 --> 00:04:22.501
"You've never faced anything like this."

00:04:22.501 --> 00:04:24.260
"Let them come."

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:27.460
His journey to becoming the planet's protector
is just beginning.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.560
During an interview with "Collider," the director
said,

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.750
"In this film, it's forming why he has a link
to humanity and why he has a link to Earth,

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:34.770
and that's emotional.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:36.199
It's not home yet to him.

00:04:36.199 --> 00:04:37.240
He's like an ex-pat here.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:40.449
He's landed, he's an alien, and he's never
been here before.

00:04:40.449 --> 00:04:44.860
That allows us to get underneath the stoicism
of what we've traditionally presented in Prime."

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:48.470
And so at this stage, he's going to look less
like the Optimus from the Michael Bay films

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.289
and much more like the G1 robot viewers saw
in "Bumblebee."

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:55.401
As well as some returning cast members, there
are some fresh faces as well.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:59.080
The new human lead characters are played by
Anthony Ramos {RAH-mos} of "Hamilton" and

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:00.169
"In the Heights."

00:05:00.169 --> 00:05:01.380
He stars as Noah.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:04.830
Dominique Fishback of "Judas and the Black
Messiah" plays Elena.

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:08.740
Despite being new to the franchise, both actors
have long histories with "Transformers," making

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.380
them perfect for these roles.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:13.790
Ramos spoke to People about his long love
of "Transformers," revealing that it was the

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:17.530
animated show "Beast Wars" that got him into
the franchise when he was growing up.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:18.530
He said,

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:20.840
"I was [in front of the TV] every week watching
'Beast Wars.'

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:24.630
So when I read the script, I saw we were gonna
have them in the movie, my head almost exploded

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:25.630
off of my body."

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:29.419
Meanwhile, Shia LaBeouf was Fishback's window
into the "Transformers" universe.

00:05:29.419 --> 00:05:31.900
The Disney Channel fan said in an interview
with "Collider,"

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:36.690
"I used to watch Shia on 'Even Stevens,' so
to watch him go from this Disney kid to this

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:40.800
movie star and being in the 'Transformers'
films, I was like, 'Oh, man, I wanna do something

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:41.800
like that!'

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.819
I couldn't imagine that almost 20 years later,
I would be doing it as well."

00:05:44.819 --> 00:05:47.720
"Rise of the Beasts" also boasts several other
notable cast members.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:52.430
The Lord of Casterly Rock himself, Peter Dinklage,
voices the villainous Scourge.

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:57.380
Ron Perlman plays the silverback Optimus Primal,
a character he portrayed before in the animated

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.880
"Transformers: Power of the Prime" series.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:03.130
Pete Davidson takes over the role of Autobot
Mirage from the late Francesco Quinn, and

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.890
Michelle Yeoh voices Airazor.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:09.340
"Optimus, we must trust each other to protect
the home we all share."

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:13.690
One character notably missing from this list
is Bumblebee, who was voiced by Dylan O'Brien

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:16.220
in his 2018 solo outing.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:19.449
O'Brien's return to the franchise hasn't been
confirmed and his commitment to other features

00:06:19.449 --> 00:06:22.090
like "Ponyboi" has no doubt been keeping him
busy.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:25.710
However, a voice role in the movie is definitely
not out of the question, and viewers may just

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:28.065
have to wait until the film is released to
get confirmation.

00:06:28.309 --> 00:06:31.861
To tell this new story, the creative team
behind "Rise of the Beasts" are introducing

00:06:31.861 --> 00:06:36.849
three new robot tribes — Maximals, Predacons,
and Terrorcons — to the existing battle

00:06:36.849 --> 00:06:39.750
on Earth between the Autobots and Decepticons.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:43.900
The introduction of these new Cybertronians
will change the course of the Autobot-Decepticon

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.630
war that viewers have seen so far.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:48.050
Lorenzo di Bonaventura explained to "Collider,"

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:51.930
"We had somewhat exhausted, I would say, [that]
battle ... So, our hope was, how do we find

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.910
a new set of villains and a new set of priorities
for the villains?"

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:58.810
However, the producer quickly noted that there
were lots of tribes and new characters from

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:02.990
the extended "Transformers" universe who had
yet to be seen on the silver screen.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:06.419
The Predacons and Terrorcons fall on the side
of the Decepticons, while the Maximals are

00:07:06.419 --> 00:07:08.290
a new tribe of heroes.

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:11.849
These new transformers turn into robotic animals
and birds.

00:07:11.849 --> 00:07:16.240
Optimus Primal is the leader of the Maximals
and transforms into a gorilla-like beast.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.810
Teasing a little more about what viewers can
expect from these animalistic heroes, Caple

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:21.360
explained to "USA Today,"

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:25.400
"In our particular film, they're these prehistoric
animals that travel through time and space,

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:26.860
and we find them here on Earth."

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:31.770
"Transformers: Rise of the Beasts" introduces
both the Predacons and Terrorcons as two new

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:35.400
factions of Decepticons, but one should be
feared more than the other.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.410
In an interview with "Collider," Caples said,

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:41.380
"When the Terrorcons enter the screen and
disrupt our movie, you're gonna feel it."

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:45.000
These robots are the main villains of the
film, and they are led by Scourge, a merciless

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:49.270
predator who takes pleasure in stealing insignias
from the fallen Autobots he defeats.

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:54.394
Caple was particularly excited about including
Scourge, who was a blank slate for big-screen viewers.

00:07:54.394 --> 00:07:55.211
He said,

00:07:55.211 --> 00:07:57.120
"It felt like Scourge was someone that was
untapped.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:01.710
That not only allowed me freedom, but it also
created this super ruthless and scary character."

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.699
Scourge's right hand is the shape-shifting
Terrorcon Nightbird.

00:08:04.699 --> 00:08:08.500
She has been adapted from the "Beast Wars"
cartoon for the movie and, according to the

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.960
director, she's had some modifications made
to her.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:14.620
She has a vehicle form that is new but also
possesses ninja traits.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.180
Teasing more about her history, Lorenzo di
Bonaventura said,

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:21.129
"What I find very interesting is that she
switched sides and now she's a Terrorcon who

00:08:21.129 --> 00:08:22.560
has joined that side of it.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:25.479
Her history is one that has had flexible alliances,
which is fun."

00:08:26.181 --> 00:08:30.510
It's pretty common for "Transformers" to explore
different locations across the globe, showcasing

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.440
how widely spread the robots have become.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:36.620
They don't just exist in cities like New York
and Chicago, they also hide out in the deserts

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:39.580
of Egypt and Jordan, as seen in "Revenge of
the Fallen."

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:44.411
Meanwhile "Age of Extinction" took viewers
off to far-flung locations like China and Iceland.

00:08:44.411 --> 00:08:46.422
"Rise of the Beasts" follows a similar pattern.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:50.880
The film traverses continents, taking viewers
to locations like New York and Peru.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:54.930
Additionally, the movie was filmed in a few
more places, including Los Angeles and Montreal.

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:58.860
However, it was the South American locations
that most excited the film's director.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.029
He revealed to "Collider,".

00:09:00.029 --> 00:09:04.160
"Very few films have been shot, not only in
Peru, but also Machu Picchu, and they opened

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:05.240
the doors for us.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:09.100
I'm grateful to collaborate with Peru and
highlight Peru's culture and the ancient civilization.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:13.261
They have beautiful landscapes and sites,
but most importantly, beautiful people, and

00:09:13.261 --> 00:09:14.660
I'm excited about that."

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:17.940
This location is no doubt going to be important
for the character of Elena.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:21.839
As a museum researcher, this may be where
she discovers one or more important artifacts

00:09:21.839 --> 00:09:23.684
relating to the Terrorcons.

00:09:23.684 --> 00:09:28.130
The "Transformers" movie franchise sprang
into action in 2007 when Shia LaBeouf played

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:30.420
Sam Witwicky, a shy but smart high school
kid.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:34.990
But, with the help of Bumblebee, Optimus Prime,
and their transforming friends, as well as

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:39.550
Mikaela Banes, Colonel William Lennox, and
Agent Simmons, he became an earth-saving hero.

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:43.839
LaBeouf returned twice more with his companions,
but in his third outing, Mikaela was replaced

00:09:43.839 --> 00:09:46.060
by his new love interest, Carly.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:49.550
This was Sam and Carly's last appearance and
director Michael Bay went on to helm a new

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:53.170
duology starring Mark Wahlberg and Nicola
Peltz-Beckham.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:57.630
After this, Travis Knight took the franchise
back a couple of decades to 1987, introducing

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:00.269
a younger Bumblebee to Hailee Steinfeld's
Charlie.

00:10:00.269 --> 00:10:04.760
"Rise of the Beasts" is set eight years after
Charlie's adventures with the Transformers.

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:08.399
Following the emotional ending of "Bumblebee,"
which saw Charlie and Bee part ways after

00:10:08.399 --> 00:10:12.190
saving the day together, Charlie chose to
stay with her family and friends, while Bee

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:14.457
had to embark on a new mission of his own.

00:10:14.457 --> 00:10:16.807
"Goodbye, Bumblebee."

00:10:17.048 --> 00:10:21.370
After his adventures with Charlie, Bumblebee's
new mission was to reunite the Autobots, and

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:24.410
it appears that in the years since, he has
done just that.

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:28.519
"Transformers: Rise of the Beasts" picks up
with the fan-favorite robots back together.

00:10:28.519 --> 00:10:32.839
Discussing how the setting of 1994 came about,
producer Lorenzo di Bonaventura explained,

00:10:32.839 --> 00:10:35.170
"We were thinking about it as a progression.

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:39.660
Bumblebee was in 1987, so then how do we move
it forward and also not run into the timeline

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:40.660
of the Bay films?

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:44.649
We had picked '94, in part because there was
great music during that time period, so it

00:10:44.649 --> 00:10:46.389
felt like that natural extension."

00:10:46.389 --> 00:10:49.890
This fits perfectly with director Steven Caple
Jr's vision for the film.

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:53.209
After reading the script, he felt very connected
to the time period and wanted to continue

00:10:53.209 --> 00:10:54.209
this story.

00:10:54.209 --> 00:10:58.290
He also noted that along with the music Bonaventura
plans to capture, there's going to be a lot

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:00.560
of '90s culture and aesthetics throughout
the film.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:04.269
So, it sounds like viewers can expect a great
nostalgia trip from "Rise of the Beasts."

00:11:04.903 --> 00:11:09.870
Steven Caple Jr. grew up watching the animated
"Transformers" TV series "Beast Wars," which

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:12.196
ran from 1996 to 1999.

00:11:12.196 --> 00:11:15.579
And since the movie takes a lot of inspiration
from the show, it's no wonder Caple found

00:11:15.579 --> 00:11:16.649
himself at the helm.

00:11:16.649 --> 00:11:17.649
He told "Collider,"

00:11:17.649 --> 00:11:22.019
"What brought me to the project was the chance
to imagine on a different level and to dream.

00:11:22.019 --> 00:11:23.820
That's what 'Transformers' means to me.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:27.339
Dealing with robots, dealing with humans,
and creating that bond, it's all about the

00:11:27.339 --> 00:11:29.920
emotion and where we can take our new characters."

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:33.760
Despite the inspiration "Transformers: Rise
of the Beasts" takes from the '90s show, not

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:37.149
every element of it is being carried over
exactly as it was.

00:11:37.149 --> 00:11:40.459
For "Transformers" fans who are familiar with
"Beast Wars," it's important to note that

00:11:40.459 --> 00:11:45.160
the 2023 movie has taken some creative liberties,
including introducing a whole new crew of

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:46.260
voice actors.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:49.700
Time travel is one element from the series
that Caple has indicated will be carried over.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:52.790
However, it won't be in the same way viewers
have seen before.

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:56.209
The movie's timeline will differ from the
one established in "Beast Wars," which is

00:11:56.209 --> 00:11:57.750
set 300 years in the future.

00:11:58.109 --> 00:12:01.860
Every director brings their own ideas and
creativity to a project.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:06.170
Michael Bay did this with the first five "Transformers"
films, putting his unique stamp on the franchise

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:11.451
and delivering on the themes of heroes and
villains, good overcoming evil, and hope overcoming loss.

00:12:11.451 --> 00:12:15.899
But moving forward from those films, Bonaventura
said Steven Caple Jr. brought a must-needed

00:12:15.899 --> 00:12:16.899
new perspective.

00:12:16.899 --> 00:12:17.785
He explained,

00:12:17.785 --> 00:12:21.095
"We were trying to accomplish a certain change
up from the movies we did with Michael [Bay].

00:12:21.209 --> 00:12:24.870
We wanna deliver a film that has the scale
and spectacle of the Bay films with the heart

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:27.699
and humor that we were able to achieve in
Bumblebee."

00:12:27.699 --> 00:12:30.970
The director's new perspective brought with
it a darker tone to the movie.

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:34.670
The fact that the main villains have the word
"terror" in their name should instantly instill

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:39.070
fear, according to the director who is planning
to take that darker energy and run with it.

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:40.070
He teased,

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:43.370
"I wanna dabble more in horror in this one
and make people jump out of their seats."

00:12:44.118 --> 00:12:45.918
You can't stop the "Transformers."

00:12:45.918 --> 00:12:50.610
After all, they've earned over $4.8 billion
at the worldwide box office, and they finally

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:53.089
got some critical cred with their last venture,
"Bumblebee."

00:12:53.089 --> 00:12:56.720
If Paramount gets its way, "Transformers:
Rise of the Beasts" won't be the last time

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:59.079
these robots take over our theater screens.

00:12:59.079 --> 00:13:02.769
In February 2022, "Collider" reported that
the official Paramount Twitter account had

00:13:02.769 --> 00:13:06.170
announced "Rise of the Beasts" would be the
first installment of a new trilogy.

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:10.150
Assuming that it does solid business, chances
are good we'll see Noah, Elena, the Maximals,

00:13:10.150 --> 00:13:12.580
and Optimus Prime back on the big screen again.

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:13.580
"I'm nobody.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:14.580
I ain't even seen nothing.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:15.832
I'm not even seeing anything right now."

00:13:15.832 --> 00:13:20.740
A CG-animated "Transformers" theatrical film
will also follow in 2024 but is separate from

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:22.100
the upcoming trilogy.

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:25.490
The upcoming animated feature will be an origin
story for Optimus Prime and Megatron.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:30.100
It will be set on Cybertron and have "Superman"
and Krypton influences, according to producer

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:32.017
Lorenzo di Bonaventura.

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:36.010
In an interview with "Collider," producer
Lorenzo di Bonaventura talked about how much

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:38.910
action viewers can expect to see in "Rise
of the Beasts."

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:43.209
He confirmed that the film will strike a nice
balance of CGI and practical elements.

00:13:43.209 --> 00:13:47.110
This means real-life stunts, which is where
Anthony Ramos and Dominique Fishback's newly

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:49.490
minted driver's licenses might come in handy.

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:52.579
Alongside a stacked cast, there's also plenty
of talent behind-the-scenes.

00:13:52.579 --> 00:13:57.930
Joining Lorenzo di Bonaventura and Steven
Caple Jr. is Joby Harold, who created the

00:13:57.930 --> 00:14:00.870
story for "Rise of the Beasts" and co-wrote
the screenplay.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:05.220
Sci-fi fans will know Harold best as the producer
behind the Disney+ series "Obi-Wan Kenobi."

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:10.590
He's also worked as a writer on DC's 2023
movie "The Flash," which is in direct competition

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:12.250
with this "Transformers" feature.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:16.170
Additionally, "Rise of the Beasts" will be
rated PG-13 like all the other movies in the

00:14:16.170 --> 00:14:17.369
"Transformers" franchise.

